  "invariant": {
    "rule": "the speech panel, the name chip and the option bubble never occlude the speaker's sprite rect — the character IS the portrait. speakerClear (20 px) is one implementation of it, not the rule.",
    "tailRule": "the TAIL is the pointer and the exception: it reaches towards the speaker and stops gap (3 px) clear of the sprite ink, measured through mount({clear}) rather than guessed from the anchor. clear is DIRECTIONAL — a down tail clears the crown, an up tail hangs the bubble below the FEET (below the head is her body), so aim an up tail at the hip/foot anchor or pass the anchor→ink-bottom distance.",
